  "limits": [
    "Single machine shared with production and ~40 other containers; the API, MinIO and SQL Server contend for 6 CPUs and 7.75 GiB of RAM, so absolute latency is a property of this host, not a capacity model.",
    "Total load time was about 11 minutes across five phases. This is a smoke-level performance check, not a soak test; nothing here says anything about behaviour over hours, memory growth, or GC under sustained load.",
    "The platform rate limit of 120 requests per minute per client key, combined with a single OIDC client identity, capped admitted work at 120 req/min. Backend saturation was therefore never reached and the backend's real throughput ceiling is unknown; what is demonstrated is that admission stays bounded and admitted latency stays bounded while 99.9 % of offered load is rejected cheaply.",
    "Read-heavy mix only: four GET endpoints (published metadata, signed-URL issue, package-run view, ~190 KB manifest document). No ingestion, upload, matching or snapshot write was driven under load.",
    "The signed download endpoint was exercised only up to issuing the signed URL; the object bytes were not fetched from MinIO under load, so MinIO was near idle throughout.",
    "Load was generated on the server over loopback, so client-side network, TLS termination at the edge and real client geography are excluded.",
    "No publication and no rollback of a publication were performed: publishing snapshot 53 is an owner decision (ADR-007) and was deliberately not taken, so 14.5's rollback leg remains open.",
    "Recovery covered one API container restart. Database, object storage and Keycloak restarts were not tested because they are shared with production."
  ],
